[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2566141015","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/100969#issuecomment-2566141015","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/100969","id":2566141015,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6Y9DRX","user":{"login":"anknetau","id":3803433,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM4MDM0MzM=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3803433?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/anknetau","html_url":"https://github.com/anknetau","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anknetau/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anknetau/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anknetau/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anknetau/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anknetau/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anknetau/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anknetau/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anknetau/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anknetau/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-12-31T05:19:12Z","updated_at":"2024-12-31T05:19:12Z","body":"Tests added in https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/100970","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2566141015/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2566369606","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/100969#issuecomment-2566369606","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/100969","id":2566369606,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6Y97FG","user":{"login":"miv391","id":49998025,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ5OTk4MDI1","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/49998025?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/miv391","html_url":"https://github.com/miv391","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/miv391/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/miv391/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/miv391/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/miv391/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/miv391/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/miv391/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/miv391/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/miv391/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/miv391/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-12-31T11:30:40Z","updated_at":"2024-12-31T11:30:40Z","body":"Your tests start from strings, e.g. \"abc\", but the actual uids are integers. So I don't think it is a problem that some random `string1 -> int -> string2` conversions produce situations where `string1 != string2`. That just means that the string1 is not a valid string representation of any integer uid. The important conversion is `int1 -> string -> int2`. int1 should always be equal to int2.\n\nAlso this \"uid://abcdefabcdefabcdefabcdef\" is an invalid uid, as according to comments in `resource_uid.cpp` the maximum length of string uid is 19 characters. \"abcdefabcdefabcdefabcdef\" is 24 characters long.\n\nAccording to this https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/83843, the `int <-> string` conversion will not be changed because of backwards compatibility.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2566369606/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":2,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2566386423","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/100969#issuecomment-2566386423","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/100969","id":2566386423,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6Y9_L3","user":{"login":"anknetau","id":3803433,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM4MDM0MzM=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3803433?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/anknetau","html_url":"https://github.com/anknetau","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anknetau/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anknetau/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anknetau/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anknetau/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anknetau/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anknetau/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anknetau/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anknetau/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anknetau/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-12-31T11:55:45Z","updated_at":"2024-12-31T12:13:04Z","body":"Thanks for your reply! Excited to be discussing this!\n\nPragmatically, I will leave the discussion about bijective functions and their benefits aside (particularly for something as important as the unique ids that glue all the objects in Godot!) but I will point out that the code is producing and accepting some funky stuff it should't.\n\n> Also this \"uid://abcdefabcdefabcdefabcdef\" is an invalid uid, as according to comments in `resource_uid.cpp` the maximum length of string uid is 19 characters. \"abcdefabcdefabcdefabcdef\" is 24 characters long.\n\nExactly why I chose it as an example - I expected it to return `-1` but it did not. I would call this a bug.\n\n> According to this [#83843](https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/83843), the `int <-> string` conversion will not be changed because of backwards compatibility.\n\nGreat! I saw that and the history, too. The current behavior is documented in the handful of tests I have added - I assumed the goal was to keep it the way it is now for sake of backwards compatibility - so the tests in https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/100970 do so.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2566386423/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2566435859","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/100969#issuecomment-2566435859","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/100969","id":2566435859,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6Y-LQT","user":{"login":"AThousandShips","id":96648715,"node_id":"U_kgDOBcK-Cw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/96648715?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips","html_url":"https://github.com/AThousandShips","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-12-31T12:59:23Z","updated_at":"2024-12-31T13:06:28Z","body":"The `uid://a` case is due to a bug I'd say, I'll write a fix soon, there's no reason IMO to preserve that, unlike the re-encoding by changing the format as mentioned in #83843\n\nHowever `uid://abc` is *not* a bug, it's simply the same as, for example, `\"012\"` -> `12` -> `\"12\"`, leading `a` is equivalent to leading zero, we *could* add a warning for invalid input but technically `uid://ab` is invalid, or at least not proper","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2566435859/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":1,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2566441285","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/100969#issuecomment-2566441285","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/100969","id":2566441285,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6Y-MlF","user":{"login":"miv391","id":49998025,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ5OTk4MDI1","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/49998025?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/miv391","html_url":"https://github.com/miv391","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/miv391/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/miv391/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/miv391/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/miv391/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/miv391/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/miv391/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/miv391/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/miv391/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/miv391/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-12-31T13:06:46Z","updated_at":"2024-12-31T13:06:46Z","body":"> The `uid://a` case is due to a bug I'd say, I'll write a fix soon, there's no reason IMO to preserve that, unlike the re-encoding by changing the format as mentioned in [#83843](https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/83843)\n\nI also noticed that it is possible that `ResourceUID::create_id()` can create an uid with value 0. It's string representation is `\"uid://\"` which will cause problems. I think this is fixable by changing the uid creation so that 0 uid will not be created. The risk of creating 0 is _very_ unlikely but I don't see any reason why that risk would be worth taking.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2566441285/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":1,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2566443151","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/100969#issuecomment-2566443151","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/100969","id":2566443151,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6Y-NCP","user":{"login":"AThousandShips","id":96648715,"node_id":"U_kgDOBcK-Cw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/96648715?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips","html_url":"https://github.com/AThousandShips","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-12-31T13:09:07Z","updated_at":"2024-12-31T13:09:07Z","body":"That would be an alternative solution, but I don't think as appropriate","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2566443151/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2566447039","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/100969#issuecomment-2566447039","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/100969","id":2566447039,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6Y-N-_","user":{"login":"miv391","id":49998025,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ5OTk4MDI1","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/49998025?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/miv391","html_url":"https://github.com/miv391","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/miv391/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/miv391/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/miv391/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/miv391/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/miv391/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/miv391/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/miv391/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/miv391/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/miv391/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-12-31T13:14:58Z","updated_at":"2024-12-31T13:14:58Z","body":"Changing this:\n\n```c++\nResourceUID::ID ResourceUID::create_id() {\n\twhile (true) {\n\t\tID id = INVALID_ID;\n\t\tMutexLock lock(mutex);\n\t\tError err = ((CryptoCore::RandomGenerator *)crypto)->get_random_bytes((uint8_t *)&id, sizeof(id));\n\t\tERR_FAIL_COND_V(err != OK, INVALID_ID);\n\t\tid &= 0x7FFFFFFFFFFFFFFF;\n\t\tbool exists = unique_ids.has(id);\n\t\tif (!exists) {\n\t\t\treturn id;\n\t\t}\n\t}\n}\n```\nso that \n\n`if (!exists) {`   --> `if (!exists && id != 0) {`\n\nwould easily prevent 0 uids. If someone ever stumbles upon an empty uid (`\"uid://\"`) it would be nice if you don't need to think whether _this_ is time when a zero uid was actually created.\n\nThis change would not break any backwards compatibility.\n\n","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2566447039/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2566447319","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/100969#issuecomment-2566447319","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/100969","id":2566447319,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6Y-ODX","user":{"login":"anknetau","id":3803433,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM4MDM0MzM=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3803433?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/anknetau","html_url":"https://github.com/anknetau","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anknetau/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anknetau/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anknetau/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anknetau/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anknetau/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anknetau/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anknetau/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anknetau/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anknetau/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-12-31T13:15:24Z","updated_at":"2024-12-31T13:16:05Z","body":"I'd be happy to contribute more to the C++ codebase, let me know how I can help. I put together those tests that pass on the current functionality https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/100970 but I can easily modify them.\n\nPersonally, I suggest that once it's possible, there should be **one and only one** valid string for each valid ID. It could enable some pretty cool things like comparison without having to parse (just by comparing strings), clarity on what's valid and being ready for any future expansions in uid without having to change the scheme.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2566447319/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2566460957","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/100969#issuecomment-2566460957","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/100969","id":2566460957,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6Y-RYd","user":{"login":"AThousandShips","id":96648715,"node_id":"U_kgDOBcK-Cw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/96648715?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips","html_url":"https://github.com/AThousandShips","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-12-31T13:35:48Z","updated_at":"2024-12-31T13:35:48Z","body":"> Personally, I suggest that once it's possible, there should be one and only one valid string for each valid ID\n\nThere is, you will never have it output leading `a`, but I don't see any reason to complicate the process and add checks for \"overlong\" UID strings, I don't think it makes sense to compare them as strings anyway, they should be operated on as integers ","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2566460957/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2566463878","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/100969#issuecomment-2566463878","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/100969","id":2566463878,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6Y-SGG","user":{"login":"AThousandShips","id":96648715,"node_id":"U_kgDOBcK-Cw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/96648715?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips","html_url":"https://github.com/AThousandShips","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-12-31T13:40:25Z","updated_at":"2024-12-31T13:41:04Z","body":"I don't think any advanced checking is needed as you would only encounter them if you intentionally make your own invalid ones, and you shouldn't really just create random uid strings, there's no use case for that I'd say\n\nWe *could* add a check but it'd just be a waste of performance IMO\n\nBut I will write a fix for the `uid://a` case","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2566463878/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2566466036","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/100969#issuecomment-2566466036","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/100969","id":2566466036,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6Y-Sn0","user":{"login":"kleonc","id":9283098,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjkyODMwOTg=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/9283098?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/kleonc","html_url":"https://github.com/kleonc","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kleonc/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kleonc/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kleonc/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kleonc/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kleonc/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kleonc/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kleonc/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kleonc/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kleonc/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-12-31T13:43:52Z","updated_at":"2024-12-31T13:43:52Z","body":"> Also this \"uid://abcdefabcdefabcdefabcdef\" is an invalid uid, as according to comments in `resource_uid.cpp` the maximum length of string uid is 19 characters. \"abcdefabcdefabcdefabcdef\" is 24 characters long.\n\nBTW looking at its usage `max_uuid_number_length = 19` is incorrect, it should be 13.\n\n`0x7FFFFFFFFFFFFFFF` -> `uid://d4n4ub6itg400`\n\nSo the max length of the number part is 13 (`d4n4ub6itg400`), it would be +6 when accounting for `uid://` (or +7 with terminating null).\n`max_uuid_number_length` is used only for creating temp buffer for converting the number, so it can be lowered to 13:\nhttps://github.com/godotengine/godot/blob/2582793d408ade0b6ed42f913ae33e7da5fb9184/core/io/resource_uid.cpp#L50-L87\n\n> The `uid://a` case is due to a bug I'd say, I'll write a fix soon, there's no reason IMO to preserve that, unlike the re-encoding by changing the format as mentioned in [#83843](https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/83843)\n\n`uid://` is already being converted to `0` so everything should work fine with it I think (aka probably not a real bug), but indeed would make more sense so `0` would produce `uid://a`[^1]. As mentioned all of `uid://`, `uid://a`, `uid://aa`, `uid://aaa`, (...) already produce `0` so changing this shouldn't be anyhow breaking. 🤔\n\n[^1]: It would make even more sense if `0` would produce `uid://0` but for whatever reason the numerical system used in the implementation firstly uses letters instead of numbers... 🙃","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2566466036/reactions","total_count":4,"+1":4,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2566467855","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/100969#issuecomment-2566467855","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/100969","id":2566467855,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6Y-TEP","user":{"login":"AThousandShips","id":96648715,"node_id":"U_kgDOBcK-Cw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/96648715?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips","html_url":"https://github.com/AThousandShips","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-12-31T13:46:42Z","updated_at":"2024-12-31T13:46:42Z","body":"Good catch will fix the length constant as well","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2566467855/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":2,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2566471547","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/100969#issuecomment-2566471547","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/100969","id":2566471547,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6Y-T97","user":{"login":"miv391","id":49998025,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ5OTk4MDI1","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/49998025?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/miv391","html_url":"https://github.com/miv391","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/miv391/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/miv391/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/miv391/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/miv391/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/miv391/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/miv391/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/miv391/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/miv391/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/miv391/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-12-31T13:52:04Z","updated_at":"2024-12-31T13:52:04Z","body":"> `uid://` is already being converted to `0` so everything should work fine with it I think (aka probably not a real bug), but indeed would make more sense so `0` would produce `uid://a`[1](#user-content-fn-1-bedef5990ccebc45c483dd1011d7566a). As mentioned all of `uid://`, `uid://a`, `uid://aa`, `uid://aaa`, (...) already produce `0` so changing this shouldn't be anyhow breaking. 🤔\n\nI briefly tested what happens when you have a uid 0. I had a scene and an attachted script. I changed script's uid to `uid://` both in the scene file and script's .uid file. It somewhat worked without any error messages, but at some point a new uid was created for the script to the scene file, but the script's .uid file was not changed. So I would say that uid 0 does not work correctly.\n\nHaving a `!= 0` check when creating uids has a non measurable performance cost, at least compared how much is the total time the function takes.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2566471547/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":1,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2566473810","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/100969#issuecomment-2566473810","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/100969","id":2566473810,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6Y-UhS","user":{"login":"anknetau","id":3803433,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM4MDM0MzM=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3803433?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/anknetau","html_url":"https://github.com/anknetau","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anknetau/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anknetau/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anknetau/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anknetau/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anknetau/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anknetau/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anknetau/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anknetau/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anknetau/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-12-31T13:55:34Z","updated_at":"2024-12-31T13:55:34Z","body":"**🎉  Folks, it's 2025 here now - happy new year! 🎉** ","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2566473810/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":1,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2566476685","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/100969#issuecomment-2566476685","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/100969","id":2566476685,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6Y-VON","user":{"login":"AThousandShips","id":96648715,"node_id":"U_kgDOBcK-Cw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/96648715?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips","html_url":"https://github.com/AThousandShips","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-12-31T13:59:44Z","updated_at":"2024-12-31T14:04:32Z","body":"Will push my fixes soon and #100970 can be rebased on top of those changes and add change the relevant test, don't think adding just a single test related to my changes is relevant if a PR is already open for adding relevant tests\n\nEdit: Realized that I need to ensure the maximum is encoded safely so will add two tests, and you can add tests in addition to that","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2566476685/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2566504749","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/100969#issuecomment-2566504749","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/100969","id":2566504749,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6Y-cEt","user":{"login":"AThousandShips","id":96648715,"node_id":"U_kgDOBcK-Cw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/96648715?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips","html_url":"https://github.com/AThousandShips","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-12-31T14:42:39Z","updated_at":"2024-12-31T14:42:39Z","body":"For completeness when it comes to a one-to-one mapping we also have that `ResourceUID.id_to_text(-1) == ResourceUID.id_to_text(-2) == \"uid://<invalid>\"`, though again you would never get a UID of `-2` by normal means","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2566504749/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":2,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2566609720","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/100969#issuecomment-2566609720","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/100969","id":2566609720,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6Y-1s4","user":{"login":"kleonc","id":9283098,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjkyODMwOTg=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/9283098?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/kleonc","html_url":"https://github.com/kleonc","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kleonc/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kleonc/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kleonc/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kleonc/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kleonc/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kleonc/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kleonc/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kleonc/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kleonc/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-12-31T17:24:38Z","updated_at":"2024-12-31T17:24:38Z","body":"> I briefly tested what happens when you have a uid 0. I had a scene and an attachted script. I changed script's uid to `uid://` both in the scene file and script's .uid file. It somewhat worked without any error messages, but at some point a new uid was created for the script to the scene file, but the script's .uid file was not changed. So I would say that uid 0 does not work correctly.\n\nHave you tried exactly the same actions/changes using a non-zero UID though? I mean just because it bugged for 0 doesn't mean it's a bug specific for 0, might be some more general issue/bug occuring for any UID.\nI'd say changing UIDs manually is rather questionable, I'd expect that I could break something by doing so, like possibly making some cache be in an invalid state or something like that. Of course would be nice if it would be properly detected and gracefully handled.\n\nAnyway, that sounds like potentially a separate issue. If you can reliably reproduce it then please open a new issue for it with all the details provided there (unless it's already reported; after quick search I found e.g. #99779 which is quite different but of similar nature (UIDs vs user manual tinkering)).\n\n> Having a `!= 0` check when creating uids has a non measurable performance cost, at least compared how much is the total time the function takes.\n\nYeah I wouldn't bother about it performance-wise, it should be fine. Still, I don't see a proper justification for disallowing 0.\n\nI don't think _\"something doesn't work for 0 so let's disallow 0\"_ is a correct approach/reasoning. Let's firstly find out what exactly fails and why, and then decide what should be done about it.","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2566609720/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2566810098","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/100969#issuecomment-2566810098","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/100969","id":2566810098,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6Y_mny","user":{"login":"anknetau","id":3803433,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM4MDM0MzM=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3803433?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/anknetau","html_url":"https://github.com/anknetau","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anknetau/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anknetau/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anknetau/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anknetau/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anknetau/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anknetau/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anknetau/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anknetau/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anknetau/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-01-01T02:25:17Z","updated_at":"2025-01-01T02:25:17Z","body":"> For completeness when it comes to a one-to-one mapping we also have that `ResourceUID.id_to_text(-1) == ResourceUID.id_to_text(-2) == \"uid://<invalid>\"`, though again you would never get a UID of `-2` by normal means\n\nThat's a great idea, I'll add it to the tests!","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2566810098/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]